{"name":"Nightingale","hex":"#5c4827","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nightingale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A hamlet in Wheatland County, Alberta, Canada, named after Florence Nightingale."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A temporary facility built at short notice during the COVID-19 pandemic, or by extension any other emergency."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nightingale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common nightingale","blocks":[{"text":"The common nightingale, rufous nightingale or simply nightingale, is a small passerine bird which is known for its powerful and beautiful song, often described as one of the most beautiful sounds in nature. An Old World flycatcher, it belongs to a group of more terrestrial species, often called chats. Its range partly overlaps with that of the more northerly thrush nightingale, a closely related species with which hybrids have occurred."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_Common_nightingale_-_Nachtegaal_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_Common_nightingale_-_Nachtegaal_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_nightingale","wikidata":"Q25393"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Luscinia_megarhynchos_Istria_01.jpg/500px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_Istria_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Luscinia_megarhynchos_Istria_01.jpg/500px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_Istria_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuscinia_megarhynchos_Istria_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Luscinia_megarhynchos_MHNT_232_HdB_Bouzareah_Alg%C3%A9rie